WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:08.045
Three settlement pods must agree on one thing: which of them runs tonight's payout batch.

2
00:00:08.045 --> 00:00:10.628
Two at once would pay every merchant twice.

3
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:18.892
Each pod opens a session with a coordination service, such as ZooKeeper or etcd, and keeps it alive with heartbeats.

4
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.869
Then each pod creates a node.

5
00:00:20.869 --> 00:00:24.536
It's ephemeral: it lives only as long as its pod's session.

6
00:00:24.536 --> 00:00:30.564
And it's sequential: the service stamps it with a revision, a number that grows with every write.

7
00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:33.262
Pod A got 7, B got 9, C got 11.

8
00:00:33.262 --> 00:00:37.287
The lowest revision leads, so pod A is the leader.

9
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:43.838
Each of the others watches only the node just before its own: B watches A, and C watches B.

10
00:00:43.838 --> 00:00:47.549
When a node goes, only the pod right behind it hears.

11
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:53.418
Pod A writes batch 17 to the ledger and sends its revision with it, as a token.

12
00:00:53.418 --> 00:00:56.152
The ledger accepts it and remembers 7.

13
00:00:56.367 --> 00:01:00.699
Now pod A freezes in a 15 second garbage collection pause.

14
00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:03.911
Its heartbeats stop, and B's and C's go on.

15
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.553
The session runs out.

16
00:01:05.553 --> 00:01:11.089
The service ends A's session and deletes its node, and the revision moves to 12.

17
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.468
B's watch fires.

18
00:01:12.468 --> 00:01:18.673
B lists the nodes again, sees its own is now the lowest, and takes over with token 9.

19
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:21.091
B writes batch 18 with token 9.

20
00:01:21.091 --> 00:01:25.097
The ledger accepts it, and its highest token becomes 9.

21
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.616
Then pod A wakes up.

22
00:01:26.616 --> 00:01:32.076
Nothing has told it yet, so it still believes it leads, and it writes with token 7.

23
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:36.469
The ledger checks: 7 is lower than 9, so it refuses the write.

24
00:01:36.469 --> 00:01:38.637
The paused leader is fenced off.

25
00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:42.615
The lowest node leads, and each pod watches the one ahead of it.

26
00:01:42.615 --> 00:01:49.471
But only the ledger can stop a leader that woke up late, so every write carries the token, and the ledger checks it.
